       ("What owners can do", "<p>Google says owners have full control: they can add or remove users, manage profile information and delete the profile. A profile can have multiple owners but only one primary owner.</p>"),
       ("What managers can do", "<p>Managers, formerly called site managers, have mostly the same access as owners. Google says the exception is that they cannot add or remove users or remove the profile. Managers can edit information, respond to reviews, manage posts and photos and download insights.</p>"),
       ("One Google Account per person", "<p>Google says each user needs their own Google Account, so nobody needs to share a password. It also notes that Google Groups cannot be added as owners or managers.</p>"),
       ("How to add an owner or manager", "<p>Go to your Business Profile, select More, then Business Profile settings, then People and access. Select Add, enter an email address, choose Owner or Manager and select Invite. Invited users can accept right away, and you receive an email when they do. Pending invites appear in the same page and can be cancelled.</p>"),
       ("Changing someone's role", "<p>In People and access, select the user, then Edit next to Access, choose the new role and save. Google notes that only owners can change access roles for other users.</p>"),
